 {"id": "TJ-DF-025", "type": "task", "priority": "P2", "status": "complete", "title": "[P2] ./install.sh --list-rule-packs exits 2 on a fresh host without PyYAML — the informational listing refuses because the shipped db.yaml cannot be parsed, poisoning &&-chained bootstrap scripts", "description": "Found 2026-09-24 dogfood on a fresh bunker-las-03 agent (bare Debian user, no PyYAML, no pip): `./install.sh --list-rule-packs` prints the pack list AND then `rule-pack-tool: refused: shipped pack .../db.yaml cannot be read (cannot parse (PackParseError: PyYAML is not installed...))`, exit 2. This contradicts the documented pack philosophy (DF-21: pack problems are a skip, not a failure) — the plain install on the same host correctly skips the pack and exits 0. Real damage: a bootstrap that runs `./install.sh --list-rule-packs && ./install.sh` aborts BEFORE installing anything — reproduced: the first install attempt on the bunker agent left ~/.local/bin/terminal-jail nonexistent while looking like a normal run. An informational listing that cannot parse one pack should print `db: unreadable (PyYAML missing)` and exit 0.", "acceptance_criteria": "On a host without PyYAML, ./install.sh --list-rule-packs exits 0, lists the db pack as skipped/unreadable with a one-line reason, and `./install.sh --list-rule-packs && ./install.sh` completes a full install.", "created_at": "2026-09-24T12:40:00-05:00", "created_by": "dogfood satellite 2026-09-24", "attempts": 0, "worker_status": "complete", "updated_at": "2026-09-24 14:18:47.221259", "worktree": "~/worktrees/terminal-jail-TJ-DF-025", "branch": "wt/TJ-DF-025", "sessions": ["tj-tick-316"], "completed_at": "2026-09-24 14:18:47.221259", "commit_hash": "d389043", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "files_changed": ["CHANGELOG.md", "README.md", "plugin/test_install.py", "plugin/test_rule_packs.py", "scripts/rule-pack-tool.py", "specs/cli.md"], "lines_added": 345, "lines_removed": 79, "worker_summary": "glm-5.3-flash@zai-glm